# Every file in this repository is executed by somebody else's coding agent on
# their own laptop. There is no such thing as a cosmetic change here, so there is
# no path without an owner.
#
# `@Arrakis-Security/security` is Arrakis Security staff only. Outside
# contributors open pull requests from forks; only this team can approve them.
#
# This file is inert on its own. It becomes an enforced rule via the branch
# ruleset described in docs/GITHUB-SETTINGS.md — "Require review from Code
# Owners", with an empty bypass list.

*                       @Arrakis-Security/security

# The prompt surface: the files that actually run on a candidate's machine.
# Listed explicitly, even though the wildcard above already covers them, so that
# a diff touching them is visibly a different class of change from a doc typo.
/skills/                @Arrakis-Security/security
/commands/              @Arrakis-Security/security
/AGENTS.md              @Arrakis-Security/security
/GEMINI.md              @Arrakis-Security/security

# Trust and supply-chain surface. A change here can switch the guardrails off.
# When there is a second staff team, make it a co-owner of these paths so
# disarming a check needs two people rather than one.
/.github/               @Arrakis-Security/security
/scripts/               @Arrakis-Security/security
/SECURITY.md            @Arrakis-Security/security
/LICENSE                @Arrakis-Security/security
/.claude-plugin/        @Arrakis-Security/security
/.codex-plugin/         @Arrakis-Security/security
/gemini-extension.json  @Arrakis-Security/security
